tlsopenssl: use SSL_get0_group_name with OpenSSL 3.2

SSL_get_negotiated_group() returns a NID only for some groups; OpenSSL 3.2
and later can name every negotiated group directly.

Part of the VPP source used for the RK3588 board build (v26.06-1-geth1test). The
tlsopenssl plugin is not built by the installer or deployed on the RK3588 board.

--- a/src/plugins/tlsopenssl/tls_openssl.c
+++ b/src/plugins/tlsopenssl/tls_openssl.c
@@ -1862,7 +1862,12 @@
 	attr->tls_profile_info.tls_version = (u16) version;
 
 	/* Get negotiated group (key agreement algorithm) */
-#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x30000000L
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x30200000L
+	const char *group_name = SSL_get0_group_name (oc->ssl);
+	if (group_name)
+	  attr->tls_profile_info.key_agreement = format (0, "%s", group_name);
+	else
+#elif OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x30000000L
 	const char *group_name;
 	int group_id = SSL_get_negotiated_group (oc->ssl);
 	if (group_id != NID_undef)
